  (text "2400-2500 BPF" (at 352.5 68.67 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e7e13615-ef31-40c6-baa1-d93ac5465949"))
  (text "keeps everything that is not\nthe ISM band off the LNA" (at 352.5 72.27 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "97207781-a490-4c8d-870e-129f898c25ee"))
  (text "-80 dBm" (at 388 52 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "56dac611-7e13-4f3d-a6d8-05a688219739"))
  (text "-83 dBm" (at 328 60.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "cb72416e-b6df-40cf-8af0-a94f5932b5c8"))
  (text "-71 dBm" (at 252 60.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "73562b20-2a1a-45ec-a9f8-538f412067ea"))
  (text "LO: the same chirp,\nnot delayed" (at 206 55 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "0291ec39-bd69-48a7-bd9f-a953d67c4517"))
  (text "5   THE RADAR ITSELF  (scaled)" (at 15 89 0) (effects (font (size 2.1 2.1) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "bb5459c1-6c7f-452a-8d6a-2ae9f973a1c7"))
  (text "Everything in the band above, written as a circuit SPICE can actually run.  Build it first:\nit shows you a beat tone before you have bought a single RF part." (at 15 93.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "74adb008-dcfd-459c-8041-ccec1faabbbc"))
  (text "chirp x delayed chirp" (at 68 107.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c6bbc591-0ea6-4ae6-bd70-86e52991adaa"))
  (text "Delay line, multiplier, then the amplifier's own filters.  Bandwidth scaled down 10x and the\ndelay up 10x, because the carrier cancels: 4 MHz over 667 ns gives the same 417 Hz as 40 MHz\nover 66.7 ns, and lets SPICE step at 10 ns instead of 20 ps." (at 68 111.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6443a11b-33b8-418a-8a55-15de78cf43c0"))
  (text "1   VIDEO AMPLIFIER  —  40 uV of audio in, line level out.  Everything else on this sheet exists to feed it." (at 15 129 0) (effects (font (size 2.1 2.1) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4cf01aae-d6e9-4950-8be5-46e158613155"))
  (text "49.9 R + 1 nF" (at 34.5 151.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7441144c-79d5-4456-8e1b-5b45d5cc3526"))
  (text "terminates the mixer and\nshorts its 2.4 GHz LO leak" (at 34.5 155.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1df3209b-8166-4a45-a5f2-329d89564a8a"))
  (text "C1 / R2" (at 92 154.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d1e99d3b-c268-466f-8861-cb82c2fe1c00"))
  (text "159 Hz high-pass" (at 92 158.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "454ab7ec-84ad-49f5-a0ac-325302670580"))
  (text "U1A  x101" (at 144 154.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d5be44e9-4c08-46cc-bc8f-f08ca6845878"))
  (text "R3 100k / R4 1k" (at 144 158.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8759b44e-7cf7-4a6e-b69a-581b845bab75"))
  (text "C2 / R6" (at 194 154.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "afade0f9-2b39-4bd5-9419-b49e303c8109"))
  (text "159 Hz again" (at 194 158.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6452a2d9-6e58-49e8-82fe-4256a97aa584"))
  (text "U1B  x11" (at 244 154.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "cff628ca-050e-4fe2-93c8-1fd4bee5a024"))
  (text "R7 10k / R8 1k" (at 244 158.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2ab73080-3847-4707-a749-45d5737cdc0f"))
  (text "R12 / C9" (at 294 154.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "86d76296-fbe2-4cd7-9f20-1c6aea0d82f8"))
  (text "15.9 kHz low-pass" (at 294 158.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6da8dbda-7bdd-4a41-b746-aaedba55d66e"))
  (text "U2B buffer" (at 346 151.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "dce31ce1-187c-4d07-a4ef-709c0ee22d00"))
  (text "unity gain, then\n100 R and 10 uF out" (at 346 155.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6c909a7e-e8a2-437e-850b-193723d44dec"))
  (text "IF  —  -78 dBm at 417 Hz, which is 40 uV pk.  This one wire carries the whole measurement." (at 40 132.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.25 1.25)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8cf32b85-6047-415f-b785-3aa4c884230b"))
  (text "Block 5 feeds the same wire the mixer does.  That is the point of it:\nyou can bring up the whole amplifier, and see a 417 Hz tone come out of it,\nwith the RF half of the sheet still in its packaging." (at 212 96 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6b7b6831-230f-4fcf-9482-071a11b84396"))
  (text "40 uV" (at 72 143.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "687af3e0-1eaa-4014-aca7-d0aae2c8e347"))
  (text "20 uV" (at 126 143.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "93c5031a-2409-4fb4-8de3-a17395c5e39b"))
  (text "2.0 mV" (at 176 143.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2949cd84-0a17-49f1-9b17-3ce281f39442"))
  (text "2.0 mV" (at 226 143.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6138493f-02cd-4b53-8440-008a085857f8"))
  (text "22 mV" (at 278 143.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7e6e0302-631b-4c3a-99fa-a07f77daaef4"))
  (text "22 mV" (at 328 143.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "1aa7953b-8b7e-4d79-8f05-b1d206675707"))
  (text "Gain is 60.2 dB measured from the amplifier's own input, but 53.6 dB from the mixer, because 50 ohm driving 49.9 ohm halves the signal before the first stage.\nThe TX-to-RX leakage arrives alongside the echo at 8 mV and leaves at 27 mV.  That 46 dB head start is what the two high-passes exist to cut down, and it is\nwhy the gain is split in two: one stage of 1100 would saturate on the leakage long before the echo ever reached the output." (at 40 171 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "77be9d7e-3c6a-4e52-b321-a97732f568a4"))
  (text "VANA powers all three op-amps here.  VREF is their input reference: on a single supply every stage swings about 5.7 V, not about 0 V." (at 40 179.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "74b21092-4d7d-4531-9c31-ccbe6c4944c1"))
  (text "3   12 V INPUT" (at 15 193 0) (effects (font (size 2.1 2.1) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "33780975-703d-437b-8b2c-f535fa617f07"))
  (text "D1  ->  R15 / C13" (at 57 209.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9aeb3fdf-9308-4378-90c7-29b9d3020ab3"))
  (text "1N5822 makes a reversed plug harmless: VPROT reads -0.11 mV,\nnot -12 V. R15/C13 then filters the buck's 150 kHz to 4 mVpp." (at 57 213.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ceeb4828-2125-465d-803e-9f7f413c9c87"))
  (text "11.58 V" (at 96 201.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2473769d-4324-40a3-ab06-7ba7cc923d77"))
  (text "2   HALF-RAIL REFERENCE" (at 15 231 0) (effects (font (size 2.1 2.1) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "3e54a59a-5bc4-46bb-9940-08c61dcf47b8"))
  (text "R9 / R10  ->  U2A" (at 57 243.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4237a4c9-93e2-4b44-96dd-05d592dfb2ff"))
  (text "VANA / 2, buffered, so the six returns inside block 1\ncannot pull the reference around." (at 57 247.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e2c9dd5e-7eb8-4dc5-b557-f0222dfd6560"))
  (text "5.7 V" (at 96 235.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "bfaed83f-ac63-4b1b-8516-2eca8f4a05c7"))
  (text "VANA and VREF are net labels: every label with the same name is one wire.\nVANA reaches block 2's divider and block 1's three op-amp rails.\nVREF reaches six points inside block 1: R2, R4, R6, R8, C9 and the buffer." (at 15 253 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "ac6efe3a-7bd2-4314-a3cf-1bc06dcac34a"))
  (text "4   SYNC DIVIDER  —  and the two channels the laptop actually records" (at 159 193 0) (effects (font (size 2.1 2.1) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "e20f7526-3936-423b-9e51-0a8805b66e95"))
  (text "ESP32 + radar_ctl" (at 185 217.75 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b0de364b-6360-415e-a67d-ecedaf911127"))
  (text "Steps the PLL, holds SYNC high for the\nup-chirp, turns the table between chirps.\nBoots with the RF off." (at 185 221.35 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "eef582fd-2bde-4b6c-9d2e-41a1301e6013"))
  (text "10k / 1k" (at 256 215.21 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "eab643dc-ae29-4e8c-858e-33839c87a270"))
  (text "3.3 V logic down to 0.3 V\nso it cannot clip the input" (at 256 218.81 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "73af80f8-13ab-46c8-8952-f3819cd231cd"))
  (text "UCA202" (at 323 216.48 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "5f00549e-ecba-4118-92c9-8e96723815b4"))
  (text "48 kHz, 16-bit, line level.\nEvery enhancement off." (at 323 220.08 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "92f4bedd-af0d-4e64-9961-4df0b54f7df0"))
  (text "A4988 + NEMA-17" (at 253 233.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "b40b3a4f-1a4e-40b1-87db-b60560ccb540"))
  (text "1/16 step, 8.889 steps per degree" (at 253 237.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "c32f72dd-32f8-4708-9e40-a88766e03b0d"))
  (text "3.3 V square" (at 236 206.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8012ba5e-011a-4e3b-950c-631a3fda3038"))
  (text "0.3 V" (at 296 207.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "f3aa68de-1635-4b71-b991-8e5da0112525"))
  (text "step / dir" (at 236 221 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "47ff8204-3b0c-4200-b16f-b88a8093601a"))
  (text "SCK / MOSI / LE, each through 33 R, all the way back up to the PLL" (at 60 185.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.05 1.05)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "00397338-4a2a-4b64-aea4-8156f13fd3cf"))
  (text "AUDIO_L  —  19 mV pk at 417 Hz" (at 328 197 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "7660b07b-afbf-4083-94ba-7ceb7b749f17"))
  (text "Left channel is the measurement.  Right channel is the clock: radar_acquire.py finds the chirp edges on it and derives T_up and the PRI\nfrom them on every block, so changing the sweep on the ESP32 needs no matching change on the laptop." (at 159 243 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "d79b192f-5fcc-4db1-b708-12893c85755c"))
  (text "SOFTWARE" (at 159 259 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8f915460-8458-4375-aa6f-9b1119a8ea2c"))
  (text "laptop" (at 369 277.94 0) (effects (font (size 1.35 1.35) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "62dec638-acae-4a8b-bed6-804a28282183"))
  (text "USB" (at 380 262 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9ed759ba-3122-4b37-8aaa-96ad903273d3"))
  (text "ground_station/radar_acquire.py, once per block of 64 chirps:\n\nread 48 kHz stereo  ->  find the sync edges (T_up, PRI)  ->  cut into 64 chirps\n  ->  FFT along one chirp   = RANGE       ->  FFT across the 64 = VELOCITY\n  ->  CA-CFAR, peak-picked  = DETECTIONS  ->  weight over azimuth = BEARING\n  ->  {range, velocity, snr} to server.py, drawn in the browser." (at 159 264 0) (effects (font (size 1.25 1.25)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a511a4f0-a1f8-4052-8481-36e023849f9f"))
  (text "HOW TO READ THIS SHEET" (at 15 268 0) (effects (font (size 1.85 1.85) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "a0cfd96a-1450-45a8-b41b-009985e31640"))
  (text "Build and bench them in this order, because each needs the one before it:\n3  first.  Everything else runs on its output.\n2  next.  Block 1 will not bias without VREF.\n1  then, driven at its IF pin by a signal generator.\n4  whenever.  It touches nothing else on the sheet.\n5  any time, in SPICE alone, before the RF parts arrive." (at 15 272 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "2b7330ed-ac44-4f25-bfb8-42a6cee346e6"))
